      "comment": "Showcase flight (2026-10-09, reshaped 2026-10-10; golden hour 18:15 with time almost stopped, timescale 1, chosen from test shots at 6:30-19:30): up the Upper Niben under the stone bridge, west through the channel south of the city to Lake Rumare, then once round the Imperial City island over the water, anticlockwise: west lake, under the Talos bridge at Weye (through its western arch at x 4450: underside 630-720 units above the water, measured in game with upward traces; the pillar at x 5200-6000 is solid), the north channel, over the wooded land bridge north-east of the city, down the east water and the Niben back to the stone bridge, over it, and climbing to ~5400 units south-east over the river with the camera tilting down for a panorama of the south. Timed to the game's main theme (Data/Music/Special/tes4title.mp3, 110.9 s; start the music with the fade-in): 110.9 s, speed per waypoint 1800-2475 units/s (calm 2050 for the first 40 s, building with the music's swell through the Talos arch at 43 s, Vilverin at 71 s, over the stone bridge at 97 s, slowing to 1800 for the panorama as the music fades). Route trimmed by ~11k units (start ~9k later, shorter final climb). The path is generated from control points (bench/routes/rumare-loop.json in the maintainers' lab, tools/shape_flight.py: smooth B-spline, resampled every 1800 units, checked for height, shore distance, the bridge gates and camera turn rates). Waypoints are x,y,z,pitch,speed. Starts at speed and fades in, fades out before the end and hovers there (no fall); the runner goes to the start before the warm-up. camlook/camtau/camsmooth: the camera aims 2.5 s ahead and turns with two-stage smoothing (no left-right hunting).",
